# Jomovate website — optional WhatsApp settings.
#
# 1. Copy this file to .env.local in the same folder (.env.local is gitignored and never committed).
# 2. Fill in either or both values below. Leave a value empty to keep its button hidden.
# 3. Run: npm run build   (the build reports "enabled" or "hidden" — it never prints the number)
#
# For the live site, add the same two names as environment variables in Netlify:
#   Project configuration → Environment variables → Add a variable
# then trigger a new deploy.
#
# Privacy: a "Chat on WhatsApp" link (https://wa.me/<number>) is public. Anyone who views the
# page source or clicks the button can see the number it points to.

# Business WhatsApp number in international format, e.g. +44 followed by the number without its
# leading 0. Spaces are allowed. A UK number starting with 0 is also accepted and converted.
WHATSAPP_NUMBER=

# Exact URL of the Jomovate WhatsApp channel, copied from WhatsApp (Channel info → Share → Copy link).
# It must start with https://whatsapp.com/channel/
WHATSAPP_CHANNEL_URL=
